  "title": "No New Construction Is Needed for the Product and Łukasiewicz Cases of a Fuzzy-Metric Problem",
  "batch_label": "62",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "Let N_0={0,1,2,...}; for x,y in N_0 and t>0 let ell(x,y)=min{x,y}, mu_t(x,y)=|x-y|/(2^t-1)-ell(x,y), q_t(x,y)=0 if x=y and q_t(x,y)=2^(mu_t(x,y)-t) otherwise, and M(x,y,t)=1/(1+q_t(x,y)). For each T in {T_P,T_L}, where T_P(a,b)=ab and T_L(a,b)=max(0,a+b-1), (N_0,M,T) satisfies every George--Veeramani fuzzy-metric axiom. Moreover, with x_n=n for n in N and psi(u)=2u/(1+u), the unchanged sequence is strictly fuzzy psi-contractive for every m,n in N and t>0, and it is not Cauchy. Hence the same M, sequence, and psi from Theorem 3.2 and Counterexample 3.4 of arXiv:2609.03372v1 answer its Problem 3 affirmatively for both requested t-norms, exactly as asserted in the frozen original claim.",
